    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d458">

                <pb facs="0630" n="506" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg506"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.51 Or 4/25</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of the Treasury</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Moss</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-03-05"><hi rendition="#italic">March 5,
                        1923</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: For the Secretary, I have the honor to
                    acknowledge the receipt of letter of Assistant Secretary Harrison (EA–894.51 Or
                    4) of March 2, 1923,<anchor n="54" xml:id="d458-f1"/> with reference to the
                    proposed loan to the Oriental Development Company of Tokyo, which loan is to be
                    guaranteed by the Japanese Government.</p>
                <p>It is noted that the Department of State has informed the National City Company
                    that, in the light of the information at hand, it offers no objection to this
                    financing.</p>
                <p>In confirmation of telephone advices, the Treasury desires to state that it
                    perceives no objection to the proposed financing. Respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">McKenzie Moss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
